6.181.m:
The son said:
'I am your son named Śiva, eager to obtain gold;
astonished by the dream obtained at night, I have come.'

The serpent said:
If you are my son, quickly release me from the bond;
[for] I have been born as a serpent because of the buried treasure of my previous birth.

6.183.m:
The glorious Mahādeva said:
Hereafter, I will declare the ninth chapter with care;
be calm and listen attentively, O daughter of the snowy mountain!

6.184.m:
